{"id":31469,"slug":"bim-the-little-donkey","title":"Bim, the Little Donkey","year":1951,"country":"France","duration":54,"spine":null,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/31469-bim-the-little-donkey","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/7f7b1e74acc6bcaed65182b64c09448b/bI2uJyZL0QRBTndH2dCxrTin60TTIG_large.jpg","description":"Featuring narration by celebrated poetic-realist writer Jacques Prévert, Albert Lamorisse’s first fiction film established his stylistic and thematic signatures: elegant simplicity, storybook-like voice-over, and empathetic concern for children and animals. Filmed on the Tunisian island of Djerba, this spirited adventure follows two boys—one poor and good-hearted, the other wealthy and spoiled—who go from rivals to friends as they set out to save a donkey from thieves. From the start, Lamorisse’s gift for bringing forth the inner lives of his nonhuman characters suffuses his art with an otherworldly magic.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Albert Lamorisse","slug":"albert-lamorisse"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Abdallah","role":null,"slug":"abdallah"},{"actor":"Messaoud","role":null,"slug":"messaoud"},{"actor":"The children of the island","role":null,"slug":"the-children-of-the-island"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Albert Lamorisse","slug":"albert-lamorisse"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Albert Lamorisse","slug":"albert-lamorisse"},{"role":"Narration written by","person":"Jacques Prévert","slug":null},{"role":"Narration written by","person":"Albert Lamorisse","slug":"albert-lamorisse"},{"role":"Narrator","person":"Jacques Prévert","slug":null},{"role":"Producer","person":"Georges Derocles","slug":null},{"role":"Photographed by","person":"André Costey","slug":null},{"role":"Photographed by","person":"Guy Tabary","slug":null},{"role":"Assistant director","person":"Roger Mauge","slug":null},{"role":"Assistant camera","person":"Wladamir Awanow","slug":null},{"role":"Assistant camera","person":"J. P. Robinot